## Updating an Existing Specification

### When Specifications Need Updates

- Clarification from user/stakeholder feedback
- Scope change approved by governance authority
- Bug found in requirements during implementation
- Quality audit finding requiring remediation

### Update Procedure

**Step 1: Create Change Request**

Document what needs to change:
- Which section(s) of spec.md need updating
- Why the change is needed
- Proposed change text

**Step 2: Run Specification Clarify (if needed)**

If update resolves ambiguity:

```bash
/speckit-clarify
```

This will guide you through clarifying the specific section.

**Step 3: Apply Changes**

Directly edit the relevant spec.md section:
- Preserve spec ID and section structure
- Update section content with clarified/corrected text
- Document change in Clarifications section with date

**Step 4: Re-validate Quality**

Run quality checklist on updated spec:

```bash
/speckit-checklist {domain}
```

Verify quality dimensions still pass after changes.

**Step 5: Update Catalog Currency**

Update "Last Updated" date in CATALOG.md entry:

```
| 005 | example-spec | Example Feature | Purpose text | Active | 2026-09-16 |
```

**Step 6: Submit for Approval**

Create PR with update:
- Link to original specification
- Document what changed and why
- Request governance review

**Step 7: Merge Changes**

After approval, merge to develop. CATALOG.md currency is now updated.

