## Catalog Maintenance

### Catalog Location

Central catalog maintained at: `.github/specs/CATALOG.md`

### Required Fields for Each Entry

| Field | Description | Example |
|-------|-------------|---------|
| # | 3-digit spec number | 001 |
| Title | Human-readable specification title | PRD Agent Consolidation |
| Purpose | One-line purpose statement | Consolidate multiple PRD agents into unified system |
| Status | Draft, Active, or Archived (canonical enum) | Active |
| Created | Date specification was created | 2026-01-15 |
| Link | Relative markdown link to spec.md | [./001-prd-agent-consolidation/spec.md](./001-prd-agent-consolidation/spec.md) |

### Currency Requirements

- Catalog must be updated within 7 days of creating a new specification
- If new spec created on Sept 16, catalog must be updated by Sept 23
- Verify "Last Updated" date in catalog metadata is within 7 days of current date

### Catalog Update Checklist

When updating CATALOG.md, verify:

- [ ] All 12+ existing specifications appear in catalog
- [ ] Entry number, slug, title match spec.md exactly
- [ ] Status field is current (Active, Archived, etc.)
- [ ] All links point to valid spec directories
- [ ] No duplicate entries
- [ ] Entries in sequential order (001, 002, 003...)
- [ ] Last Updated date is within 7 days of any changes

### Catalog Validation

Verify catalog completeness using the validation checklist:

```bash
# Run directory audit to verify structure
./.specify/scripts/bash/audit-specs.sh
```

Then manually verify:
- All directories in `.github/specs/` appear in CATALOG.md
- No broken links in catalog
- Numbering is sequential (001-013+)
- No duplicate entries

